WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:05:00.000
Speaker 1: Welcome everyone. We're using this 30-minute session to review project progress, unblock outstanding items, and align on next steps. I'll start with a quick recap of the milestones we committed to last week and then hand over to each owner for updates. Please be concise so we can cover everything.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:10:00.000
Speaker 2: Thanks. On the backend side, we've completed the API redesign and integration tests. There were a few performance regressions which we fixed by optimizing queries and adding an index. I'll follow up with the PR link and sample metrics in the chat. We still need to finalize caching strategy.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:15:00.000
Alice: On the frontend, the new dashboard layout is ready and responsive. We encountered a layout shift in mobile when images load; we added placeholders and lazy loading which reduced CLS. The remaining tasks are accessibility fixes and wiring live data streams.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:20:00.000
Bob: For testing and QA, we completed smoke tests for the main flows and created new end-to-end scenarios for the most common user journeys. Test flakiness dropped after stabilizing the async waits. Next week we'll automate nightly runs and attach artifacts to the CI pipeline.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:25:00.000
Carol: Regarding deployment, the staging rollout was successful but we observed a small memory spike under load. We've scheduled an investigation with the infra team; initial theory points to a library holding references. We'll add better monitoring and an alert to catch repeats.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:30:00.000
Speaker 1: Closing remarks — action items: (1) Backend to propose cache TTL and schema for review, (2) Frontend to push accessibility fixes by EOD Wednesday, (3) QA to finalize nightly pipeline, (4) Infra to run memory root cause analysis. We'll reconvene in the weekly sync. Thanks everyone.
